9861	{"artifactId":"LLD-b135647ed951c0c1-s1","entry":{"id":"review-fcee4712fb2fc4487c53891b2c010c75","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:15:09.360Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed ac1–ac5 cover every upstream requirement for this standalone Story.","evidence":"Searched repository docs and .insrc artifacts for the Story hash and title; found the LLD but no independent standalone Story requirements or acceptance baseline. The adjacent s9 DEF confirms preservation of identity semantics, but cannot establish this Story's complete scope. The analyzer returned incomplete, mostly off-topic evidence. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-b135647ed951c0c1-s1.json, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"Attach the originating Story text and confirm the acceptance baseline before implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"gh_auth currently has status, switch and logout with 30-second limits; status converts text, while githubIdentities directly requests JSON hosts.","evidence":"account.ts defines exactly these three ops with limitS: 30; buildAuthStatus calls ghConvert. githubIdentities calls run(['gh', 'auth', 'status', '--json', 'hosts'], { timeoutMs: 15_000, maxBytes: 256 * 1024 }). [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts]","action":"Preserve these existing operation definitions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Spawn errors, timeouts, non-zero exits and cut captures have distinct ToolFailure kinds.","evidence":"ghFailureOf returns 'missing-tool' for spawn errors and 'timed-out' for timeouts, but both an unmarked cut capture and an ordinary non-zero exit return 'rejected'. Network failures return 'unreachable'. The design's invariant claiming distinct kinds is false. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Describe distinct diagnostic cases rather than distinct kinds, and include unreachable in the documented non-zero-exit outcomes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A new module-private custom builder can reuse the existing family executor without changing shared execution infrastructure.","evidence":"OutSpec.custom accepts build(ctx): Promise<Record<string, unknown> | ToolResult>. BuildContext contains stdout, stderr, input, deps and truncated. shape propagates failed ToolResults or wraps returned fields with op. defineGhFamily automatically registers each op's limit and approval class. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Use the existing custom output path and limitS registration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Recording a second auth status op requires an unresolved coverage representation or corresponding input-check changes.","evidence":"GhCoverageRow already documents 'op (or ops, comma-separated)'. gh-coverage.test.ts uses (row.op ?? '').split(','); gh-inputs.test.ts also splits that field and checks fields across the covering ops. Thus op: 'status,hosts' is already supported without a second command row or shared schema redesign. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/coverage.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-coverage.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-inputs.test.ts]","action":"Specify changing the existing row to op: 'status,hosts'; remove the deferred representation decision and unnecessary input-check changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The implementation and test change-site inventory is sufficient for the existing gh suites to pass.","evidence":"gh-family-tools.test.ts iterates every ghAuthTool op and asserts seen.has(`${tool.id}.${op.name}`). gh-output-schemas.test.ts similarly asserts every family op is exercised. Both derive cases from _family-rows.ts, whose auth fixtures currently omit hosts. Adding isolated hosts tests does not satisfy those sweeps. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/_family-rows.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-family-tools.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-output-schemas.test.ts]","action":"Add a hosts case to ROWS3 in _family-rows.ts, with JSON stdout, exact argv, approval class and 15-second limit; include this fixture in the change inventory.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new hosts shape can coexist with status without a persistent-data migration or relationship diagram.","evidence":"buildOutputSchema creates a union whose members contain literal op discriminators. Existing status returns an array, while custom hosts can return a host-keyed map under its own member. The execution path returns transient ToolResult data and introduces no storage writes. The design states host-to-account-array containment and preserves extra account fields; no persisted ownership or cross-entity relationship changes require an ERD. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts]","action":"Keep status's schema intact and explicitly allow additional account properties in the new member.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Providing the new registry capability without migrating githubIdentities respects the adjacent s9 boundary.","evidence":"The s9 LLD assigns the githubIdentities seam migration to s9 and identifies the gh account-family JSON capability as a prerequisite. This design changes the tool and its tests, leaving the direct identity caller untouched. Consequently, its identity-status descriptions are future integration expectations rather than effects of this Story alone. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md, src/understanding/identity.ts]","action":"Explicitly identify s9 as the owner of consuming hosts and translating ToolFailure into identity lookup statuses.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Checking ctx.stdout.length > 262144 enforces the promised 256 KB byte limit.","evidence":"ghExec decodes captured bytes using bytesToText before invoking the custom builder. runShellBytes counts Buffer chunk lengths, whereas the proposed builder checks the decoded string's length. UTF-8 account fields can exceed 262144 bytes while remaining below 262144 JavaScript code units, so oversized JSON would be accepted. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Check Buffer.byteLength(c.stdout, 'utf8') against 256 * 1024 before parsing; retain rejection of capture truncation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed JSON host/account shape is confirmed against actual supported-gh output.","evidence":"The existing consumer expects a hosts object of account arrays and reads state and login, supporting the proposed compatibility target. Neither that parser nor the design supplies captured output from a gh version supporting this flag, so actual producer compatibility remains unconfirmed. [files: src/understanding/identity.ts, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Add a sanitized fixture captured from a supported gh version and validate it against both the builder and output schema.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The planned timeout and byte-boundary tests reliably prove the stated acceptance criteria with the existing fake gh.","evidence":"The proposed operation has a 15-second timeout, but _fakegh.ts implements sleep mode as 'sleep 5', which finishes before that deadline. The planned byte-boundary cases also omit multibyte output, allowing the specified stdout.length implementation to pass despite violating the byte limit. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/_fakegh.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-timeouts.test.ts, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Specify a fake process that exceeds 15 seconds or a controlled timeout seam, and add valid multibyte JSON cases at and above the UTF-8 byte boundary. Keep the listed acceptance mapping and extend the existing family fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":4,"low":6,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T11:15:09.360Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
