543	{"artifactId":"LLD-b135647ed951c0c1-s1","entry":{"id":"da7fedd1cdbe4f1c92985e8e85f99c22","actor":{"id":"insrc:design.story","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:18:38.640Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"83723a6863d79863fd300176fbf7ace22a9d32fd4983ffe5c090d0ae63a08f51"},"outcome":{"result":"ok","summary":"Applied the findings of daemon review round 1 (1 HIGH, 4 MED): byte-length size check, diagnostics wording, coverage row, family fixtures, timeout and multibyte tests."},"addresses":[]}}
9185	{"artifactId":"LLD-b135647ed951c0c1-s1","entry":{"id":"review-001d551503413e7a3c83da19fcf2e981","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:18:48.140Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The inferred ac1–ac5 cover all upstream requirements for this standalone Story.","evidence":"Repository searches for the hash and title found the LLD and its artifact record, but no independent originating Story acceptance baseline. The artifact explicitly states: 'The Story record has no acceptance criteria'. The analyzer returned an off-topic, incomplete bundle with empty upstream evidence. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-b135647ed951c0c1-s1.json, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Attach the originating Story userValue and establish ac1–ac5 as its acceptance baseline.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing gh_auth operations use 30-second limits and text conversion for status; githubIdentities independently requests JSON hosts with the stated bounds.","evidence":"account.ts defines status, switch and logout with 'limitS: 30'; buildAuthStatus calls ghConvert. githubIdentities calls run(['gh', 'auth', 'status', '--json', 'hosts'], { timeoutMs: 15_000, maxBytes: 256 * 1024 }). Its body reads account.state and account.login and subsequently requests each successful account's node_id. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts]","action":"Preserve the existing operation definitions and identity consumer.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new hosts operation can reuse the custom-output executor without changing shared infrastructure.","evidence":"OutSpec.custom accepts build(ctx): Promise<Record<string, unknown> | ToolResult>. BuildContext supplies stdout, stderr, input, deps and truncated. shape propagates failed ToolResults or adds the literal op to returned fields. defineGhFamily automatically registers approval classes and limits. The existing auth operation list contains no hosts operation. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts]","action":"Use the existing custom builder and limitS registration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Updating the existing coverage row and adding a ROWS3 hosts fixture integrates the operation with the existing inventories and sweeps.","evidence":"coverage.ts currently records auth status with op 'status'. Both gh-coverage.test.ts and gh-inputs.test.ts use '(row.op ?? \"\").split(\",\")'. The family and output-schema sweeps derive cases from ROWS3 and assert that every operation is exercised. The proposed fixture therefore addresses the required inventory change without adding a tool. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/coverage.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-coverage.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-inputs.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/_family-rows.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-family-tools.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-output-schemas.test.ts]","action":"Apply the proposed coverage and fixture changes; retain the 69-tool assertion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The host-keyed account map can coexist with the existing status array without a stored-data migration, and the relationship documentation is adequate.","evidence":"buildOutputSchema constructs a union with a literal op discriminator for each operation; custom results are transient ToolResult data. Existing status retains its array schema. The design specifies host-to-zero-or-more-account containment, required account fields, preservation of additional fields, and compatibility through separate op names. No persisted relationship or UX change requires a companion diagram. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/account.ts, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Keep the status member intact and explicitly allow additional account properties in the hosts schema. No additional visual is necessary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding the capability without migrating githubIdentities preserves the adjacent s9 ownership boundary.","evidence":"The s9 LLD assigns the githubIdentities seam migration to s9 and states that missing registry shapes must be reported to the family Story rather than approximated. This design changes the auth family and its tests, leaving the consumer migration outside its implementation steps. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S009/LLD.md, src/understanding/identity.ts, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Clarify that identity-status effects describe the later s9 integration. Its adapter must reconcile s9's documented raw-command seam with this typed output.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing execution failures retain the documented diagnostics, while the builder can enforce the byte limit and reject malformed output.","evidence":"ghFailureOf checks spawn errors, timeout, abort, signals, stderr overflow and capture truncation before successful exit; non-zero exits become missing-signin, unreachable or rejected. defineGhFamily returns these failures before calling shape. Thus cut output receives the existing capture-cap message, while uncut oversized output reaches the proposed Buffer.byteLength check. executor.ts validates successful data against outputSchema. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain the existing capture-cut diagnostic and perform the byte and shape checks before returning parsed data.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed schema matches output from a gh version supporting auth status --json hosts.","evidence":"identity.ts supports the proposed consumer-facing map and account fields, but this is parser evidence rather than producer evidence. The design explicitly reports that no supported-gh output was observed and supplies no captured producer fixture. Repository reads and the incomplete analyzer bundle did not establish actual producer compatibility. [files: src/understanding/identity.ts, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Provide a sanitized capture from a supporting gh version and validate it against the builder and output schema.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The planned tests map each locally defined criterion to meaningful checks, including the revised timeout and multibyte boundaries.","evidence":"The acceptance table maps ac1–ac5 to command, limit, diagnostics, schema, compatibility and coverage checks. _fakegh.ts can emit arbitrary fixture stdout and sleeps five seconds. helpers.ts exports registerGhLimits, whose later registrations replace earlier limits, enabling the proposed lowered-limit timeout test. Existing family sweeps check argv, approval class, timeout and output schema. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/_fakegh.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-timeouts.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-family-tools.test.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/gh-output-schemas.test.ts, docs/standalone/add-json-hosts-form-gh-auth-E20261027b135647e/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Import registerGhLimits from helpers.ts, where it is exported, and restore the 15-second limit in finally. Implement the listed tests; their execution and the upstream acceptance baseline remain unverified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-27T11:18:48.140Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
